  "body": "**Stacked on #437** (#418), which is on #433 (#417) and #432 (#416). Until those merge, this diff includes their commits; the #419 work is 68bd14a5. Part of #363.\n\n## The citation gate (the issue's precondition)\nBefore any code, the issue required a primary-source citation that chained Fanuc G32 blocks keep spindle synchronization. Found in *FANUC Series 0i-TD/0i Mate-TD USER'S MANUAL (For Lathe System)*, B-64304EN-1/01, Part II:\n- **§3.4 \"Continuous Threading\", p.34:** consecutive threading blocks keep \"the synchronism with the spindle\" at \"the joint between blocks wherever possible\", so the lead and shape can change midway.\n- **§3.2 \"Constant Lead Threading (G32)\", WARNING 6, p.32:** a threading block that follows a threading block starts \"without waiting for detection of the one-spindle-rotation signal\".\n- **§3.2, pp.29-31:** G32 cuts tapers (`G32 X41.0 Z29.0 F3.5`). Up to 45° the lead F is taken along Z.\n\nThe manual was read from a public third-party mirror of Fanuc's PDF (https://www.slideshare.net/slideshow/fanuc-0itd-users-manualpdf/259106078), for behaviour only. The Haas G32 reference (cited in #363) agrees. **LinuxCNC G33 stays unconfirmed:** its docs don't say whether a chained G33 waits for the index again, so no LinuxCNC post may declare the capability.\n\n## What changed\n- **Parameters.** The infeed plan gains `ThreadInfeed.dips` with interval, height and length. An interval of 0 means off, which is the default.\n- **Shape of a dip.** A dip is a radial lift on **roughing passes only**. Each ramp stays under 45°, keeping the lead on Z.\n  - **Never placed in:** the first or last lead, or the finishing, spring or #418 repeat passes.\n  - **Height:** no more than every dipped pass's depth of cut.\n- **New CL segment.** A dip is a variable-radius XY half-turn: the axial travel is still exactly half a lead, but the end radius differs from the start.\n- **Marking.** The thread record carries `chip_break_dips`: `DIP 1` in the stream, `ChipBreakDips` as a post property, and a project cache key only when set. The section carries `PARAM ChipBreakDips`. If dips are on but the record can't be attached, the kernel refuses, so a dip is never laid unmarked.\n- **Post capability flag.** The engine refuses dips by name for any script without `continuousThreading = true`. Only `fanuc-lathe.cps` declares it, with the citation in its header.\n  - It writes each dip segment as `G32 X Z F`.\n  - It refuses by name a segment that doesn't continue a G32 chain, is steeper than 45°, or goes deeper than its plunge.\n  - **G76 refuses dips by name.**\n- **Verdict.** `thread_warnings` checks every chain for phase (equal axial advance per half-turn), depth, slope and placement. Any breach is a Gouge, which blocks the post.\n- **UI.** Three rows on the Passes tab.\n- **Defaults are byte-identical.** With dips off there is no stamp byte, project key, stream word or PARAM.\n- `docs/decisions/419-thread-dips.md`\n\n## How tested\n- **New motion `turning_thread_dips`** (8 tests):\n  - dips off lay the plain path bit for bit;\n  - a dip is never deeper than its pass;\n  - the phase is unchanged across the chain;\n  - placement and slope rules hold;\n  - a repeated depth cuts whole;\n  - the verdict is silent on laid dips;\n  - the verdict convicts each broken law (first/last lead, finishing pass, deeper, phase shift, steep). Temporarily disabling the laws made this test fail.\n  - refusals by name.\n- **New app `lathe_post_thread_dips`** (6 tests):\n  - the golden `thread_g32_dips.nc`;\n  - the posted chain keeps the plain thread's Z words and lead;\n  - G76 refuses;\n  - a post without `continuousThreading` refuses;\n  - the lathe script refuses a bent dip;\n  - dips ride the command, the stream and the project file.\n- **Existing suites green:** the turning thread, infeed and G76 suites, `inverted_post`, `lathe_post*`, `project_roundtrip`, `conformance`, and all cl and post tests. No existing golden changed.\n- `clippy -D warnings --all-targets` on motion, post, cl, app and ui is clean.\n\n## Not exercised (draft)\n- **Machine check:** a run on a lathe simulator or machine.\n- **GUI check:** the Passes-tab rows. The #416 test kit covers the neighbouring rows.\n\nChangelog: Threading: optional in-pass chip-break dips on roughing passes, posted as continuous G32 X Z F segments by the Fanuc lathe post (#419)\n\nFixes #419\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
